WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.674 --> 00:00:05.257
- Here we are in the
Hoh Valley Rainforest.

00:00:07.071 --> 00:00:09.904
This is a cathedral, my cathedral.

00:00:12.959 --> 00:00:15.728
In this forest is the quietest place

00:00:15.728 --> 00:00:17.821
in the entire United States,

00:00:17.821 --> 00:00:21.070
and it's only one square inch in size.

00:00:21.070 --> 00:00:23.903
My mission is to keep it that way.

00:00:30.728 --> 00:00:32.062
I'm Gordon Hempton.

00:00:32.062 --> 00:00:33.686
I'm a sound tracker.

00:00:33.686 --> 00:00:37.376
I travel the globe in
search of vanishing sounds,

00:00:37.376 --> 00:00:39.664
including the most endangered of all,

00:00:39.664 --> 00:00:41.664
which is simply silence.

00:00:44.414 --> 00:00:47.581
Noise pollution is nearly inescapable.

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:51.127
The Hoh Valley is the quietest,

00:00:51.127 --> 00:00:55.294
least noise-polluted place
in the entire lower 48.

00:00:58.742 --> 00:01:00.448
I don't know if I can save silence,

00:01:00.448 --> 00:01:02.615
but I know that I can try.

00:01:07.335 --> 00:01:10.650
So it was 12 years ago, 2005 Earth Day,

00:01:10.650 --> 00:01:14.083
that I hiked up the Hoh River Valley.

00:01:14.083 --> 00:01:16.126
It took three miles just to escape

00:01:16.126 --> 00:01:19.135
the noise of the parking lot.

00:01:19.135 --> 00:01:21.626
That's when I was looking
in every direction

00:01:21.626 --> 00:01:23.793
for which way I should go.

00:01:25.387 --> 00:01:28.845
I saw the elk trail, love
to follow their advice

00:01:28.845 --> 00:01:32.095
because they love quiet just like I do;

00:01:34.058 --> 00:01:36.891
and they led me right to the spot.

00:01:38.830 --> 00:01:42.997
It's just through that tree,
then off into the woods.

00:01:47.446 --> 00:01:49.844
I defend this one square inch of silence

00:01:49.844 --> 00:01:53.261
by doing both quiet and noise monitoring.

00:01:59.922 --> 00:02:01.983
When a noise intrusion occurs,

00:02:01.983 --> 00:02:04.007
I locate the noise maker,

00:02:04.007 --> 00:02:07.590
send them a letter,
and ask for compliance.

00:02:09.926 --> 00:02:12.078
This matter is urgent.

00:02:12.078 --> 00:02:15.183
Within ten years, it's
likely that there will be

00:02:15.183 --> 00:02:18.766
no quiet places left
unless we take action.

00:02:23.487 --> 00:02:26.243
When I first started, I did not think

00:02:26.243 --> 00:02:29.576
silence would go extinct in my lifetime;

00:02:31.833 --> 00:02:34.798
and if that happens,
the quiet will disappear

00:02:34.798 --> 00:02:37.798
and the wildlife will be devastated.

00:02:39.815 --> 00:02:41.892
The One Square Inch of Silence foundation

00:02:41.892 --> 00:02:45.958
is pressing our politicians
to pass a single piece

00:02:45.958 --> 00:02:49.804
of legislation that will
designate Olympic National Park

00:02:49.804 --> 00:02:53.971
as the world's first quiet
park, off-limits to aircraft.

00:02:55.483 --> 00:02:57.483
All things are possible.

00:02:59.358 --> 00:03:03.136
The Earth is here and it's beautiful;

00:03:03.136 --> 00:03:07.303
and, for me, it all starts
here in the Hoh Valley.

